//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// ICY × ICT22 FRAMEWORK v1.1.17  —  clean visual ICT engine display  (NON-GATING)
// =============================================================================
// v1.1.17 REVIEW CLEANUP (28 September 2026) · runs on Core v1.0.8 or v1.0.9
//   * Side column: CISD captions use the same monospace font as every other side caption.
//   * The Focus grab caption stays on its short grab mark; only live captions join the column.
//   * HTF key areas join timeframes with "/" (15m/1H +FVG), so " + " never reads as polarity.
//   * Dealing range captions read DR H / DR EQ / DR L.
//   * HUD: the structure % row appears only when the score is shown (no "VIEW focus focus").
//   * Legend lists the current chart language (bull / bear gaps and reactions, DRAW, range, dim).
//   * Cleanup: one PD context stream, unused tuple values, a dead parent-guard write, the
//     redundant FVG.touched flag and comments orphaned by the move to Core. Engine unchanged.
// v1.1.16 NARRATIVE SIDEBAR (27 September 2026) · reuses Core v1.0.8
//   * Removed the projected HTF candles and their display-only Daily OHLC history.
//   * Paired HTF engine retained; C1-C4 labels now print on the actual chart candles.
//   * Active reaction, MSS/CISD, draw and footprint labels have sidebar priority.
//   * Nearby unclaimed Raw PA context is capped and dim; historical captions stay local.
// v1.1.15 VISUAL CLEANUP (27 September 2026) · requires Core v1.0.8
//   * Confirmed owner-close HTF FVG -> iFVG key areas, with separate DRAW identities.
//   * Fill-only shading switch and adjustable opacity, default 10/100.
//   * Spaced side-label column with price connectors and room before projected candles.
//   * MSS P/D FVG reactions: light green bullish, red bearish; failed arrays stay grey.
// v1.1.14 RUNTIME FIX (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.7 (unchanged)
//   * v1.1.13 stopped on bar 31 (array.get: index 0, size 0). The swing liquidity list, HTF key
//     areas, PD streams and CISD+ map lists were each held twice: once in an indicator variable and
//     once in the Core's pdCfg / cmReg objects. On TradingView those were separate lists, so the
//     Core's picks indexed a list the indicator never filled. Each list now has one owner (pdCfg /
//     cmReg) and the indicator reads it through that owner on every bar.
// v1.1.13 COMPILE-SIZE FIX 2 (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.7
//   * v1.1.12 compiled to 101,820 tokens (limit 100,256). Display and selection helpers move to
//     Core v1.0.7, which does not count toward this script's size: HUD / legend cells, the
//     line-style setting, curve arc points, zone time lines, PD array tooltips, the structure
//     score, swing picks / cluster names and HTF key-area picks. Behaviour is unchanged.
// v1.1.12 COMPILE-SIZE FIX (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.6 (unchanged)
//   * v1.1.11 compiled to 105,752 tokens (limit 100,256). Chart gaps are now painted in two
//     places - when a gap leaves the registry and in the last-bar pass - instead of after every
//     state change (the paint was inlined about twenty times). Every drawn gap is still painted
//     from its final state, so the chart is unchanged.
//   * The colour-opacity fade added in v1.1.11 is removed (it was inlined ~45 times); element
//     transparency works as in v1.1.10.
// v1.1.11 DISPLAY SETTINGS (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.6 (unchanged)
//   * Every chart element has its own display row: show, colour, line style (Solid / Dotted /
//     Dashed) and width. Groups 8-12: View, levels & zones, narrative, chart FVGs and projected
//     HTF candles (body, border and wick colours for bull and bear). Defaults keep the v1.1.10
//     look; a colour's opacity setting now fades its element.
//   * New switches: grab / invalidation / DRAW lines, entry array, narrative CISD, market shift,
//     raid arc, outcome marks, iFVG boxes, key-area C.E., PD zones and early-exhaustion marks.
//   * The BPR switch draws or hides the box only: the narrative BPR is tracked either way.
//     A live narrative's OB / breaker stay out of the PD zone map even while their lines are off.
//   * EMA 20 / 50, RSI and Williams %R removed completely (inputs, plots, study gates, HUD row).
//     The HUD shows an SMT row while the SMT study is on.
// v1.1.10 STUDY VIEW (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.6
//   * Focus keeps raw PA arrays visible in a dim study grey until a grab activates a
//     narrative; that narrative colours only its own arrays. Completed narratives and their
//     arrays return to the same dim grey (both dims have their own switch; colour "Dim").
//   * HTF1 / HTF2 breakers can qualify: Core seeds breaker provenance on every stream.
//   * Daily-fallback parent CISD starts on its own Daily candle (Core PDBar.b0 anchor).
//   * Engine-off parent CISD: a doji continues a run but no longer extends the anchor life,
//     matching the PD engine exactly.
//   * Key-area H/L tolerance renamed (keyHlTol): no shadowing of the grab tolerance.
// v1.1.9 HTF KEY AREAS (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.5
//   * HTF1 / HTF2 FVG key areas default on, independent of active narratives.
//   * Two groups by default: nearby levels on either side, exact live draws protected.
//   * Higher timeframe owns the outline; a light band marks the shared intersection.
//   * Same-polarity members keep their own bounds, touches and owner-close invalidation.
//   * H/L proximity describes ERL / IRL location; no grade or new entry rule.
//   * Separate display / target controls; source IDs avoid equal-label invalidation.
//   * Code-health pass removes obsolete selector state and three unused range slots.
// v1.1.8 ARRAY FOCUS (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.4
//   * No label grades. Focus protects the grab, shift, selected reaction, invalidation,
//     nearest obstacle and draw. Supporting overlaps share the primary tooltip.
//   * FVG / iFVG visuals are lightly shaded boxes in both Focus and All arrays views.
//   * Failed-OB captions distinguish a recorded sweep / structure break from an OB flip.
//   * Formation, role activation and response are separate; holds are not touch penalties.
//   * Visibility never selects entries, targets, responses, alerts or ledger outcomes.
//   * Capacity cleanup retires drawings without releasing array ownership or selector state.
// v1.1.7 CHART CLEANUP (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.3
//   * Removed the PD matrix HUD, complete limit-entry study, and session-box module.
//   * Price drawings, projected candles, arcs and optional EMAs use the main chart scale.
//   * Main HUD has one fewer row; PD responses and narrative mapping remain active.
//   * Publish Core v1.0.3, update its import version, then add a fresh chart instance.
// v1.1.6 COMPILER FIX (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.2
//   * Pass float(na) for mt at every imported f_pdAdd call (BPR / NDOG / NWOG).
//     Explicit typing resolves CE10189 at the library boundary.
//   * Uses the same Core v1.0.2 publication as v1.1.5.
// v1.1.5 REVIEW FIXES (26 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.2
//   * BPR reuse requires both contributing gap timestamps, not equal prices alone.
//   * Continuation LIMIT studies follow the selected CONT mode and its source window.
//   * Completed owner candles control parent-CISD invalidation. With the PD engine on,
//     the parent display and forming anchors mirror the same stream as the PD matrix.
//   * Core retains the HTF run-start anchor / full guard; no chart-bar resurrection.
//   * Companion checks require both Pine sources and reject incomplete validation.
// v1.1.4 REVIEW CLEANUP (25 September 2026)  ·  imports ICYFrameworkCore v1.0.1
//   * The narrative's OB / breaker come from the chart PD stream, which now runs whenever narratives
//     are mapped: they no longer vanish with the PD engine switch or the OB / breaker detector toggles.
//   * OB / breaker lines start on the order-block candle, not on the displacement bar.
//   * A narrative BPR reuses the engine's matching BPR; arrays a live narrative draws to the live bar
//     (entry OB, breaker, BPR) are not repeated as expanded zones until its retest.
//   * DRAW candidates are established HTF1 arrays (iFVG, OB, breaker, BPR, RB, MB) - never the VI /
//     VOID? / IFG? / ROB? proxies; the draw kind comes from the draw search, not from its name.
//   * One call site for the narrative step (compiled size). The SMT symbol is requested only while
//     SMT is on. Liquidity grabs have alerts. Legacy CONT events fire only in the legacy CONT mode.
//   * Removed dead state: Seq.endIdx, PDSession.started, htfVisC1Seq, the unused native bar index and
//     a duplicate OB search at the shift (Core v1.0.1 removes its never-read fields).
// v1.1.3 MODULAR FULL BUILD (25 September 2026)
//   PD response, CISD map and reusable visuals now compile in ICYFrameworkCore.
//   Inputs, timing, native requests, narratives and study switches stay in this indicator.
//   Publish the supplied helper privately, then set the import username below.
//   Built-in `second` shadowing warning fixed with `secondIndex`.
// v1.1.2 COMPILED-SIZE REFACTOR (25 September 2026)
//   Shared drawing / stream factories and looped HUD cells reduce repeated calls.
//   Full input help lives in comments; Settings retain concise operational reminders.
//   All engines, array families, optional studies, defaults and alerts retained.
// v1.1.1 COMPILER FIX (25 September 2026)
//   Rename the reserved identifier `text` in the study marker and PD zone renderer.
//   Complete v1.1.0 feature set retained.
// v1.1.0 FULL REVIEW BUILD (25 September 2026)
//   Unified source-TF responses, causal CONT, qualified OB -> breaker ancestry,
//   locked ranges, obstacle / draw provenance, native Daily/Weekly fallback,
//   RB / MB / VI / BPR / implied-gap and void proxies / reclaimed blocks / open gaps.
//   User-requested optional studies: ordered chain, structural percentage,
//   early exhaustion, sessions, Fibonacci, EMA/oscillator/SMT filters and LIMIT markers.
//   Checklist percentages are NOT probabilities. Limit markers are an OHLC study,
//   not broker orders. C-path labels are hypotheses, not inferred intrabar ordering.
//   Legacy notes below describe earlier versions; v1.1.7 removes the limit/session modules.
// MERGE OF
//   ICY_FRAMEWORK v1.1.3 (some_icy_tea concept map)  — narrative engine, delivery
//     marks, liquidity-generation ranges, HUD, CISD line visual
//   ICY_FRAMEWORK v1.0.0                               — narrative outcome engine
//   ICT22 PRODUCTION v1.3.1 · CISD HTF CONTEXT         — v2.6.0 FVG rendering for
//     context gaps and HTF FVGs, H/L grouping, CISD+ array map, parent HTF FVGs
//   TTrades "Candle 2 Closure" (C2 / C3 / C4, continuation vs reversal closure,
//     0.5 equilibrium)                                  — chart C1-C4 tags
//   MMXM (market maker buy / sell model)                — side-of-the-curve engine
//
// RAW PA ARRAYS (detected on every timeframe; the registry keeps up to 80 recent gaps within
//   400 bars): SIBI / BISI and their inversions use light FVG / iFVG boxes. Focus keeps them in
//   a dim study grey until a grab activates a narrative, which colours only its own arrays;
//   completed narratives return to the dim grey. Turn Focus off for full-colour arrays.
//   CISD+ map, parent CISD and swing liquidity remain available.
// MODES (context only - each tells a different price-action narrative, none gates the arrays)
//   HTF CONTINUATION    live HTF1 candle holding beyond the previous candle's body 50% arms the
//                       nearest array on its side ("· CONT")
//   LIQ. GRAB           the reversal narrative below (MSS Premium / Discount entry array = box)
//   MMXM                curve engine inside the grab narrative (arcs optional)
//
// THE GRAB NARRATIVE (HUD rows ① - ⑦), drawn in the some_icy_tea chart language
//   (1) HTF ARRAY       HTF FVG under the grab · the swept HTF1 swing pool
//   (2) LIQ. GENERATION tight range that builds resting liquidity      grey box
//   (3) GRAB            an HTF1 swing BSL / SSL is taken                raid arc
//   (4) MARKET SHIFT    close through the CISD open or the MSS swing    💡 Market Shift
//                       + gaps of the manipulation leg that invert      purple +iFVG boxes
//   (5) ENTRY ARRAY     MSS +/-FVG or iFVG (filled box, Premium / Discount) · OB / Breaker
//                       (thin grey line) · BPR. Its retest starts the delivery.
//   (6) MMXM CURVE      engine: the manipulation leg qualifies as the first side of the curve
//                       (HUD MMBM / MMSM), anchors the iFVG / BPR claims, supplies the origin
//                       draw. Arcs optional. A raw price-action grab still maps (1) - (7).
//   (7) DRAW            nearest eligible HTF1 swing / HTF array beyond min R;
//                       else the MMXM curve origin; else a projection
//   Delivery marks: Breakaway · Measuring · Exhaustion Gap (light boxes) · IOFED · Propulsion
//
// REMOVED (by request)     PD matrix HUD, limit-entry study, session boxes / rails / tags,
//                          position boxes, Pay the Trader, side-of-the-curve tags and
//                          projected HTF candles
// CHANGED (by request)     every CISD (narrative, parent, CISD+ map) = thin grey line
//                          + grey label · FVG / iFVG arrays = light boxes, the
//                          MSS P / D reaction is emphasized · HTF FVGs = grouped key
//                          areas · liquidity = external HTF1 swings driven by the ICY
//                          state engine (grab -> narrative) · OB-type arrays = thin grey line
// NOT PORTED               the ICT22 raid -> MSS -> protected-FVG model, its grading
//                          and lifecycle HUD (budget: one narrative engine only).
//                          Parent CISD, C-sequence and HTF FVGs are context, never
//                          entry conditions.
//
// DESIGN
//   * Visual framework; no limit-entry study or broker orders. Every module is
//     toggleable and non-gating; the sequence mapper only links modules into the narrative.
//   * Bar-close evaluation: every state change - swing sweeps, grabs, shifts, FVG
//     birth / mitigation / inversion, array mapping, retests, outcomes, pivots and
//     parent-stream bookkeeping - commits on confirmed chart bars only, so alerts
//     and history agree. The open candle only moves live drawing edges.
//   * HTF context comes from completed HTF candles. The parent CISD is dashed
//     "forming" while only the open parent candle trades beyond its anchor, and
//     solid once a parent candle CLOSES beyond it. The pending anchor survives
//     intervening candles until confirmed, replaced by a newer run, or stale.
//   * Narrative outcomes: after the array retest, the draw vs the grab extreme. Both inside
//     one candle = AMBIGUOUS unless the candle's open settles it; a draw on the retest candle
//     counts only when that candle opened through the retest price.
//   * Ownership: every drawing has one owner. A narrative deletes everything it
//     owns, including FVG drawings retired from the registry; its arrays stop extending
//     once it resolves. HUD statistics come from an outcome ledger bounded by the setup
//     window, not by drawing retention.
//   * CISD overlaps: one line per cluster, drawn at the highest-timeframe owner's
//     level (parent > CISD+ ladder > chart / narrative).
//   * v1.0.2: a parent candle completes on the confirmed close of its own last chart
//     bar (HTF close), not one chart bar later; pending parent-CISD anchor life is an
//     input; optional premium / discount gate on the entry array (ICT22 style);
//     every direction loop uses a positive 0..1 counter.
//   * v1.0.3: an HTF FVG is mitigated only after the chart bar that completed it;
//     the PD gate reads the entry price and filters while selecting (FVG -> iFVG -> OB);
//     a parent-CISD anchor cannot confirm past its life; CISD overlaps cluster across
//     both directions (highest timeframe wins, absorbed anchors in the tooltip); the
//     projected panel keeps its full candle count at the parent close.
//   * v1.0.4: CISD clusters are centered on their final highest-timeframe owner
//     before nearest-per-side selection; absorbed narratives cannot override that
//     owner's direction. Charts without a valid enabled pairing project native Daily
//     candles, including on charts above Daily. This fallback is display-only.
//   * v1.0.5: chart-TF FVGs drawn = SIBI / BISI (three same-colour candles) and the
//     MSS entry array tagged Premium / Discount; narrative iFVGs stay. Casual gaps are
//     still tracked, so one that inverts can become the entry iFVG. No grab label (the
//     arc stays). Slim HUD. The dealing-range P/D tag on every gap is gone.
//   * v1.0.6: liquidity = EXTERNAL 3-candle HTF1 / HTF2 swing highs and lows (BSL / SSL),
//     no longer every HTF candle's high and low; chart-TF internal pivots only time the MSS.
//     HTF FVGs are off by default and, while hidden, are not used as draw targets. Legend off.
//   * v1.0.7: grabs arm on HTF1 swings only; an HTF2 swing is drawn only when it groups into
//     an HTF1 swing's label (ATR distance). Pay the Trader and limit orders are gone: the
//     narrative runs GRAB -> SHIFT -> ARRAY -> retest -> DELIVERY -> draw / fail. MMXM
//     side-of-the-curve arcs when the manipulation leg qualifies; narrative arrays drawn in
//     the some_icy_tea chart language (filled entry array, grey iFVG, edge-line gaps).
//   * v1.0.8: arrays map raw PA on every timeframe whatever the modes do (lines over boxes:
//     bull / bear FVG lines, purple iFVG lines; the MSS P / D entry array stays a box). HTF
//     continuation mode (live HTF1 vs the previous body 50%). Curve tags removed, arcs optional.
//     Swing lines farther than the display cap are hidden unless they are a live draw. Setup
//     history Auto scales the narrative window with the chart; continuation falls back to Daily
//     candles on unpaired intraday charts.
//   * v1.0.8.2: Daily continuation uses the confirmed prior Daily body and chart close;
//     inverted delivery gaps can transfer to the opposite narrative; inversion clears stale
//     entry / P-D styling; a live swing DRAW reserves a slot before nearest-level selection.
// =============================================================================
indicator("ICY × ICT22 FRAMEWORK v1.1.17", shorttitle = "ICY×22", overlay = true, scale = scale.none, max_bars_back = 5000, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_polylines_count = 100)

// Runs on the existing Core v1.0.8 publication (/2). Core v1.0.9 is an optional cleanup with the
// same exports this script uses; after publishing it, raise the publication number below.
// /2 is a publication number, not the semantic version. Price objects force the main pane's scale.
import ThamiP/ICYFrameworkCore/2 as core


// =============================================================================
// 1 · INPUTS
// =============================================================================
string GRP_CORE = "1 Core"
string GRP_PAIR = "2 Pairing"
string GRP_LIQ  = "3 Liquidity"
string GRP_HTF  = "4 HTF"
string GRP_PDA  = "5 PD arrays"
string GRP_SEQ  = "6 Narrative"
string GRP_DEL  = "7 Delivery"
string GRP_VIEW = "8 View"
string GRP_DLVL = "9 Display · levels & zones"
string GRP_DNAR = "10 Display · narrative"
string GRP_DFVG = "11 Display · chart FVGs"
string GRP_CSEQ = "12 Display · chart C-sequence"
string GRP_HUD  = "13 HUD"

// Full help (i_tz): The Today Only history boundary is read in this timezone.
string i_tz        = input.string("America/New_York", "Model timezone", group = GRP_CORE, tooltip = "Timezone for setup-history boundaries.")
int    i_atrLen    = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 1, group = GRP_CORE)
// Full help (i_setupHist): Only grab narratives that begin inside this window are mapped and counted. Auto scales with the chart: today up to 15m, 5 days up to 1H, 20 days up to 4H, everything above. The ICT core arrays are mapped on every timeframe whatever this is set to.
string i_setupHist = input.string("Auto", "Setup history", options = ["Auto", "Today Only", "2 Days", "3 Days", "5 Days", "10 Days", "All Loaded"], group = GRP_CORE, tooltip = "Auto: today <=15m; 5 days <=1H; 20 days <=4H; all above. Raw arrays stay active.")
// Full help (i_keepSeq): Upper bound on completed drawings. Expanded modules may retire older drawings sooner to reserve object capacity; the outcome ledger is retained.
int    i_keepSeq   = input.int(12, "Completed setups kept", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = GRP_CORE, tooltip = "Drawing cap; older drawings may retire sooner. Ledger retained.")

bool map_on_1       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map1")
string map_chart_1  = input.timeframe("1",   "LTF 1m",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map1")
string map_htf1_1   = input.timeframe("15",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map1")
string map_htf2_1   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map1")
bool map_on_2       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map2")
string map_chart_2  = input.timeframe("2",   "LTF 2m",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map2")
string map_htf1_2   = input.timeframe("30",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map2")
string map_htf2_2   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map2")
bool map_on_3       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map3")
string map_chart_3  = input.timeframe("3",   "LTF 3m",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map3")
string map_htf1_3   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map3")
string map_htf2_3   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map3")
bool map_on_4       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map4")
string map_chart_4  = input.timeframe("4",   "LTF 4m",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map4")
string map_htf1_4   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map4")
string map_htf2_4   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map4")
bool map_on_5       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map5")
string map_chart_5  = input.timeframe("5",   "LTF 5m",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map5")
string map_htf1_5   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map5")
string map_htf2_5   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map5")
bool map_on_6       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map6")
string map_chart_6  = input.timeframe("10",  "LTF 10m", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map6")
string map_htf1_6   = input.timeframe("60",  "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map6")
string map_htf2_6   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map6")
bool map_on_7       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map7")
string map_chart_7  = input.timeframe("15",  "LTF 15m", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map7")
string map_htf1_7   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map7")
string map_htf2_7   = input.timeframe("420", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map7")
bool map_on_8       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map8")
string map_chart_8  = input.timeframe("30",  "LTF 30m", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map8")
string map_htf1_8   = input.timeframe("240", "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map8")
string map_htf2_8   = input.timeframe("420", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map8")
bool map_on_9       = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map9")
string map_chart_9  = input.timeframe("60",  "LTF 1H",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map9")
string map_htf1_9   = input.timeframe("420", "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map9")
string map_htf2_9   = input.timeframe("720", "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map9")
bool map_on_10      = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map10")
string map_chart_10 = input.timeframe("240", "LTF 4H",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map10")
string map_htf1_10  = input.timeframe("720", "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map10")
string map_htf2_10  = input.timeframe("D",   "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map10")
bool map_on_11      = input.bool(true,  "", group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map11")
string map_chart_11 = input.timeframe("D",   "LTF 1D",  group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map11")
string map_htf1_11  = input.timeframe("W",   "HTF1",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map11")
string map_htf2_11  = input.timeframe("3M",  "HTF2",    group=GRP_PAIR, inline="map11")

// Full help (i_hlPerSide): Limits liquidity LEVELS per side, not setups. The nearest unswept HTF1 swings can arm a mapped grab; one narrative per side is live at a time. A live swing DRAW reserves one display slot; remaining slots show the nearest swings. This display priority does not change grab eligibility.
int    i_hlPerSide    = input.int(2, "Swing levels per side", minval = 1, maxval = 2, group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "Levels per side. Live DRAW reserves a slot; nearest swings fill the rest.")
float  i_hlClusterAtr = input.float(0.12, "Merge nearby HTF1 swings (chart ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = GRP_LIQ)
// Full help (i_h2Near): An HTF2 swing within this distance of a drawn HTF1 swing is named in its label (e.g. 15m SSL + 1H SSL). Farther HTF2 swings stay hidden and never arm a grab.
float  i_h2Near       = input.float(0.35, "HTF2 swing groups into an HTF1 swing within (chart ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "Nearby HTF2 joins an HTF1 label; it cannot arm a grab.")
// Full help (i_hlMaxDist): Display only: a swing farther from price than this many average HTF1 candle ranges is not drawn. A live narrative's draw is always drawn; grabs still arm on the nearest swings.
float  i_hlMaxDist    = input.float(3.0, "Hide swings farther than (× HTF1 avg range)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 30.0, step = 0.5, group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "Display distance only. Live DRAW always shown.")
// Full help (i_hlKeepParent): Newest HTF1 swing levels kept live (highs and lows together). HTF2 swings are kept until taken, for grouping only.
int    i_hlKeepParent = input.int(12, "HTF1 swing levels retained", minval = 4, maxval = 30, group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "HTF1 highs and lows combined. HTF2 retained for grouping.")
// Full help (i_showDol): While the latest confirmed HTF1 C2 sequence has not failed (xC2), its draw on liquidity - C1's far extreme - reads '· DOL' on its swing line. A live narrative's draw reads '· DRAW'.
bool   i_showDol      = input.bool(true, "Tag the TTrades DOL", group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "DOL: active C2 target at C1 far extreme. DRAW: narrative target.")
// Full help (i_sweep): Any Breach: any trade through a relevant H/L. Wick Rejection: the grab bar must close back on the level's side.
string i_sweep        = input.string("Any Breach", "Grab qualifies on", options = ["Any Breach", "Wick Rejection"], group = GRP_LIQ, tooltip = "Breach: trades through. Rejection: closes back on the level side.")
int    i_intLen       = input.int(2, "Internal swing strength (MSS)", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = GRP_LIQ)
int    i_right        = input.int(18, "Context right extension (bars)", minval = 4, maxval = 80, group = GRP_LIQ)

// Full help (i_pFvgMax): Total groups, normally two: nearest area and the nearest on the other side. Live FVG draws reserve their exact group beyond distance / tap filters; two live draw groups can exceed a budget of one. Hard maximum four groups.
int    i_pFvgMax   = input.int(2, "HTF FVG key areas shown", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Total key areas. Live FVG draws reserve slots; nearby areas cover both sides.")
float  i_pFvgNear  = input.float(2.5, "HTF FVG in-play distance (parent range)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 8.0, step = 0.25, group = GRP_HTF)
float  i_pFvgHL    = input.float(0.25, "FVG / H-L proximity (parent range)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Tags a bullish gap at/below SSL or a bearish gap at/above BSL. Location only; no grade or gate.")
bool   i_pFvgTap   = input.bool(true, "Keep tapped HTF FVGs until invalidated", group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "All tested members: grey. Mixed groups retain per-member status in the tooltip. Live draws stay visible.")
bool   i_pFvgDraw  = input.bool(true, "Allow HTF FVG draw candidates", group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Target search may choose a confirmed live HTF FVG beyond minimum R. Independent of key-area visibility; entry selection is unchanged.")
// Full help (i_cisdLadder): Chart plus up to two exact-multiple ladder frames below the parent.
int    i_cisdLadder = input.int(2, "CISD map LTFs", minval = 1, maxval = 3, group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Chart plus up to two exact-multiple frames below the parent.")
int    i_cisdSlots  = input.int(1, "CISD lines per side", minval = 1, maxval = 3, group = GRP_HTF)
int    i_cisdSwingN = input.int(3, "CISD extreme swing lookback", minval = 0, maxval = 12, group = GRP_HTF)
float  i_cisdClust  = input.float(0.25, "CISD nest tolerance (chart ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, group = GRP_HTF)
float  i_cisdNear   = input.float(6.0, "CISD nearby window (chart ATR)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 30.0, step = 0.5, group = GRP_HTF)
int    i_cisdKeep   = input.int(8, "Live CISDs kept / timeframe", minval = 2, maxval = 20, group = GRP_HTF)
// Full help (i_pendMax): A pending parent-CISD anchor (open of the latest opposite-colour HTF1 run) survives intervening candles until an HTF1 close confirms it, a newer run replaces it, or this many HTF1 candles pass after the run.
int    i_pendMax    = input.int(8, "Parent CISD anchor life (HTF1 candles)", minval = 2, maxval = 40, group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Opposite-run open expires this many HTF1 candles after the run.")
// Full help (i_cont): The live HTF1 candle (native Daily on unpaired intraday charts) holding (closing, on each confirmed chart bar) above a bullish previous candle's body 50% arms bullish continuation; below a bearish previous candle's body 50% arms bearish continuation. The nearest array on that side, still beyond the 50% level, is tagged · CONT. Context only: arrays are mapped either way.
bool   i_cont       = input.bool(true, "HTF continuation mode", group = GRP_HTF, tooltip = "Uses group 14 qualification. Legacy: previous body 50%; raw arrays always active.")

float  i_fvgMin  = input.float(0.05, "Min FVG size (×ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = GRP_PDA)
string i_mtBasis = input.string("Body", "OB Mean Threshold of", options = ["Body", "Range"], group = GRP_PDA)
int    i_accLen  = input.int(12, "Liquidity generation: min bars in range", minval = 4, maxval = 100, group = GRP_PDA)
float  i_accMult = input.float(1.5, "Liquidity generation: max height (×ATR 50)", minval = 0.2, step = 0.1, group = GRP_PDA)

bool   i_seqOn    = input.bool(true, "Map narratives (grab -> shift -> array -> draw)", group = GRP_SEQ)
string i_shiftBy  = input.string("Either", "Market Shift on", options = ["Either", "CISD", "MSS"], group = GRP_SEQ)
float  i_disp     = input.float(0.0, "Shift candle min body (×ATR, 0 = off)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = GRP_SEQ)
int    i_shiftWin = input.int(30, "Grab -> Shift window (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = GRP_SEQ)
// Full help (i_entrySrc): Auto: displacement FVG; if none within 3 bars of the shift, the narrative iFVG, then the OB.
string i_entrySrc = input.string("Auto", "Entry array", options = ["Auto", "FVG", "iFVG", "OB"], group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "Auto: FVG, then iFVG after 3 shift bars, then OB.")
// Full help (i_entryAt): Where price must trade for the entry array to count as retested (ARRAY -> DELIVERY). The Premium / Discount tag and gate read the same price. No order is placed.
string i_entryAt  = input.string("Proximal", "Array retest at", options = ["Proximal", "CE / MT"], group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "Retest price also defines the leg P/D tag and gate.")
// Full help (i_pdGate): Off: Premium / Discount is a tag only. On: only arrays whose RETEST price (proximal edge, or C.E. / MT) sits below the displacement leg's 0.5 (long) or above it (short) are eligible; the FVG -> iFVG -> OB fallback order still applies. Pair with Shift candle min body 0.5 for ICT22-style displacement.
bool   i_pdGate   = input.bool(false, "Entry array must sit in discount (long) / premium (short)", group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "Long retest below leg EQ; short above. Off: tag only.")
int    i_entryWin = input.int(40, "Shift -> retest window (bars)", minval = 3, maxval = 300, group = GRP_SEQ)
int    i_stopPad  = input.int(2, "Invalidation beyond the grab (ticks)", minval = 0, group = GRP_SEQ)
// Full help (i_minRR): R = retest price to invalidation (just beyond the grab extreme). A narrative measure only.
float  i_minRR    = input.float(1.5, "Draw must sit at least (R)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "R = distance from retest to invalidation.")
// Full help (i_fallR): Used when neither an HTF1 swing nor the MMXM curve origin sits beyond the minimum.
float  i_fallR    = input.float(3.0, "No draw found -> project (R)", minval = 1.0, step = 0.5, group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "Fallback after eligible swing/array and curve-origin targets.")
int    i_tradeWin = input.int(300, "Max bars delivering after the retest", minval = 10, maxval = 5000, group = GRP_SEQ)
// Full help (i_mmxm): After the market shift, a manipulation leg that spans the minimum bars and range and steps (a lower high into a sell-side grab, a higher low into a buy-side grab) is the first side of the curve (HUD MMBM / MMSM): it anchors the narrative iFVG / BPR claims and supplies the origin draw. Otherwise the narrative still maps from the raw price-action grab. Nothing is gated.
bool   i_mmxm     = input.bool(true, "MMXM curve engine", group = GRP_SEQ, tooltip = "Qualified manipulation leg anchors curve, iFVG/BPR claims and origin draw.")
int    i_mmxmBars = input.int(10, "Curve: min leg bars", minval = 4, maxval = 300, group = GRP_SEQ, inline = "mm")
float  i_mmxmAtr  = input.float(2.0, "min leg (×ATR)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.25, group = GRP_SEQ, inline = "mm")

// Full help (i_bgBars): The first delivery SIBI / BISI left untouched this long is the Breakaway Gap; later ones are Measuring Gaps (three marks per narrative).
int    i_bgBars   = input.int(6, "Breakaway / Measuring: untouched for (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 50, group = GRP_DEL, tooltip = "First untouched delivery gap: breakaway; later gaps: measuring. Max three marks.")
int    i_exhBars  = input.int(2, "Exhaustion: gap within (bars) of the draw", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = GRP_DEL)

// ── 8 View: Focus, shared colours, labels ────────────────────────────────────
bool   i_focus = input.bool(true, "Focus on active narratives", group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Display only. Off restores all arrays. Entry selection, targets, responses and outcomes are unchanged.")
int    i_focusExtra = input.int(2, "Supporting PD marks in focus", minval = 0, maxval = 6, group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Related context has priority; nearby Raw PA context can fill spare slots. Overlaps share the reaction tooltip; proxies remain available as obstacles.")
bool   i_focusHistory = input.bool(true, "Completed narratives in focus (dim)", group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Completed narratives and their arrays stay in the dim study colour. Off hides them. Outcome statistics are retained.")
bool   i_focusRaw = input.bool(true, "Raw PA arrays in focus (dim)", group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Unclaimed SIBI / BISI and iFVGs stay visible in the dim study colour; a grab-activated narrative colours only its own arrays. Off hides them.")
bool   i_arrayShade = input.bool(true, "Array shading", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "shade")
int    i_arrayOpacity = input.int(10, "Opacity / 100", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "shade", active = i_arrayShade, tooltip = "Fill only: 0 is transparent, 100 is solid. Active primary zones use this opacity; supporting, tested and history fills are fainter. Borders, lines and labels keep their own styles.")
color  C_BULL  = input.color(#008F87, "Bull", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v1", tooltip = "Direction colours: C-tags, the HTF body 50% line, PD zones and the HUD. Tested / dead: tapped key areas, failed gaps and tested zones.")
color  C_BEAR  = input.color(#D65F36, "Bear", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v1")
color  C_GREY  = input.color(#66758C, "Tested / dead", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v1")
color  C_DIM   = input.color(#B2B5BE, "Dim", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v2", tooltip = "Dim: Focus study colour for raw PA before a grab and for completed narratives. Text: tags and HUD text. Live state: HUD state.")
color  C_TXT   = input.color(#787B86, "Text", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v2")
color  C_SHIFT = input.color(#FFA000, "Live state", group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v2")
string i_lblSz = input.string("Small", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v3")
string i_fvgSz = input.string("Tiny", "FVG label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = GRP_VIEW, inline = "v3")
int    i_lblGap  = input.int(2, "Label gap (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 12, group = GRP_VIEW)
bool   i_cleanLabels = input.bool(true, "Separate side labels", group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Align active side captions in one spaced column. Dotted connectors identify the unchanged price levels. Uses Label size above.")
float  i_sideSpacing = input.float(1.0, "Side label spacing", minval = 0.5, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.1, group = GRP_VIEW, active = i_cleanLabels)
bool   i_sideRaw = input.bool(true, "Nearby Raw PA side labels", group = GRP_VIEW, active = i_cleanLabels)
int    i_sideRawMax = input.int(1, "Raw gap labels per direction", minval = 1, maxval = 2, group = GRP_VIEW, active = i_cleanLabels and i_sideRaw, tooltip = "Additional unclaimed FVG/iFVG context. Live reactions and one footprint per narrative have separate priority.")
float  i_sideNear = input.float(2.0, "Nearby context distance (chart ATR)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.5, group = GRP_VIEW, tooltip = "Display only. Limits supplementary Raw PA gaps and unrelated PD context; active narrative levels remain visible.")

// ── 9-12 Display: one row per chart element = show · colour · line style · width ──
// Box rows style the border. Array shading above controls fills only; dim states stay fainter.
// ── 9 Display · levels & zones ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Full help (i_showHL): Liquidity = 3-candle HTF1 swing highs (BSL) and lows (SSL): the middle candle trades beyond both neighbours. Registered when the right-hand candle closes, drawn from the chart bar that printed the extreme. Only HTF1 swings are drawn, arm grabs and serve as draws. An HTF2 swing is never drawn on its own: it joins an HTF1 swing's label when it sits within the HTF2 grouping distance. Chart-TF internal swings only time the MSS.
bool   i_showHL     = input.bool(true, "Swing liquidity", group = GRP_DLVL, inline = "l1", tooltip = "Confirmed 3-candle HTF1 swings. HTF2 joins nearby labels only.")
color  C_LIQ        = input.color(#787B86, "", group = GRP_DLVL, inline = "l1", active = i_showHL)
string ST_LIQ       = core.f_sty(input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dotted", "Dashed"], group = GRP_DLVL, inline = "l1", display = display.none, active = i_showHL))
int    W_LIQ        = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = GRP_DLVL, inline = "l1", display = display.none, active = i_showHL)
// Full help (i_pFvg): Display confirmed HTF1 / HTF2 FVGs as compact key areas in both views. Same-polarity overlaps share the higher-timeframe outline and one common band. Display settings never change target eligibility.
